# mlops snapshot-data --check) — any git-driven line-ending conversion (Windows'
# core.autocrlf=true converts LF->CRLF on checkout) changes their bytes and therefore
# their sha256 depending solely on which OS/config checked them out, breaking the
# fingerprint check for reasons that have nothing to do with the data actually changing.
# `-text` disables line-ending conversion unconditionally, so every checkout gets the
# exact bytes stored in the git blob.
